msgid "I3C device descriptor to reattach"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:1916
msgid "``u8 old_dyn_addr``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:1915
msgid "previous dynamic address of the device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:1916
msgid ""
"This function reattaches an existing I3C device to the bus when its dynamic "
"address has changed. It updates the bus address slot status accordingly: - "
"Marks the new dynamic address as occupied by an I3C device. - Frees the old "
"dynamic address slot if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:1924
msgid ""
"0 on success, or a negative error code if reattachment fails (e.g. -EBUSY if "
"the new address slot is not free)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:2151
msgid "check if any device can wake the system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:2152
msgid "I3C master controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:2153
msgid ""
"Iterate over devices on the bus and return true if any device has system "
"wakeup enabled and IBI enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:2156
msgid ""
"Whether a device is enabled for system wakeup is user space policy, settable "
"at any time through the device's power/wakeup sysfs attribute, so the answer "
"is only stable once user space is frozen.  Call this from a system suspend "
"callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/i3c/master-driver-api:7: ../drivers/i3c/master.c:2162
msgid "true if any device may wake the system via IBI, false otherwise."
msgstr ""

